{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213422,"nonce":"hjJzz1BTnh1wpJhACo/2lQ5CAZA=","title":"Caribou bundle format and two-layer Api schema","message":"Own format modelled on .hatch: manifest, language-tagged Module sections\n(wren/wlbc@7, haxe/hl, zyn:\u003cgrammar\u003e/hir), Api, NativeLib per target,\nResource, Source, Docs. Module formats are versioned per adapter, never by\nthe bundle. hatch itself is untouched; the Wren adapter installs .hatch\npackages as Wren's module format.\n\nApi has two layers. Runtime types: HashLink's type table as TypeDesc carries\nit, enforced by the bridge on every call; ash emits it from the .hl for free,\nWrenLift emits what sema knows and dyn elsewhere. Declarations: per-language\nsource interfaces; generated by the Haxe compiler for Haxe packages (keeps\nwhat HashLink erases, type parameters above all); hand-written declaration\nfiles for Wren packages, as Haxe externs validated by the Haxe compiler.\nA Wren package without one arrives in Haxe as Dynamic.\n\nWorld::install(bundle). No registry in the first release.","files":null}]}